// Campus building list — Polytechnic University of the Philippines, Sta. Mesa.
//
// The campus is three separate compounds:
//   "A. Mabini"      — the main campus
//   "NDC Compound"
//   "M.H. Del Pilar"
//
// Every building record carries its own compound name. The compound is therefore
// never a separate question the student answers — confirming the building
// already determines the compound.
//
// Still to be supplied:
//   latitude, longitude — map coordinates for each building
//   floors              — how many floors the building has
//   rooms               — the room numbers on each floor, keyed by floor
//
// Fields per building:
//   name        the building's name as students know it
//   compound    one of the three compound names above
//   latitude    decimal degrees, north positive
//   longitude   decimal degrees, east positive
//   floors      number of floors
//   rooms       floor number -> list of room numbers on that floor

[
  // --- A. Mabini Campus ------------------------------------------------------

  // The Main Academic Building is divided into wings: North Wing and South Wing.
  // Its rooms are numbered with the floor as the first digit — Room 420 is on
  // the 4th floor. The wing is part of how a room is located, so when the room
  // list below is filled in, it must distinguish North from South.
